 #### 📖 SciPy Reference: Discrete PMF

**`scipy.stats.rv_discrete.pmf`**

pmf(k, *args, **kwds)


Probability mass function at `k` of the given RV.

**Parameters:**

| Param | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `k` | `array_like` | Quantiles (values at which to evaluate the PMF) |
| `arg1, arg2, arg3, …` | `array_like` | Shape parameter(s) for the distribution (see docstring of the instance object for more information) |
| `loc` | `array_like, optional` | Location parameter (default=0) |

**Returns:**

| Name | Type | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `pmf` | `array_like` | Probability mass function evaluated at `k` |

---

> **Note:** `k` is the set of unique values our column has.
> Compute it with `k = np.unique(dfsurvey['trstplt'])` or manually with `np.min()` / `np.max()`.
> The PMF gives the percentage of probability each unique value has of appearing in our sample (n=500 rows).   
